{
  "_readme": [
    "Siri phrases for the App Shortcuts provider (TidybyteShortcuts.swift).",
    "",
    "These do NOT live in Localizable.xcstrings. App Intents resolves them",
    "through Tidybyte/Resources/AppShortcuts.xcstrings, which build-catalog.mjs",
    "generates from this file. Putting them in the app catalog instead is silent:",
    "the keys are never looked up, coverage reads 100%, and Siri answers in",
    "English in all 20 languages. That mistake shipped once already.",
    "",
    "Each key is the FIRST phrase of a `phrases:` array in Swift, verbatim.",
    "The array holds every phrase for that shortcut — the key is repeated as the",
    "first element, and the rest are alternate utterances Siri also matches.",
    "",
    "TWO HARD RULES for every translated phrase:",
    "  1. It must contain the literal token ${applicationName}. Apple requires",
    "     every App Shortcut phrase to name the app; without it Siri will not",
    "     offer the shortcut at all.",
    "  2. The token may move. It is the app's display name in the sentence, so",
    "     put it wherever that language naturally puts it.",
    "",
    "The token is NOT a format specifier — no %-style substitution happens, so",
    "do not escape it, reorder it, or translate its contents.",
    "",
    "`en` is the source of truth and is checked against the Swift file by",
    "extract.mjs. Every other language has the same number of phrases, in the",
    "same order, as `en`.",
    "",
    "Vocabulary is taken from the app's own catalog rather than translated fresh,",
    "so Siri says the same words the screen behind it shows. The shortcut titles",
    "in Localizable.xcstrings (\"Start a Cleanup Session\", \"Show Storage\",",
    "\"Clean Screenshots\", \"How Much Can I Free Up?\", \"Show My Savings\") are the",
    "reference for each language's phrasing."
  ],
